1
00:00:08,277 --> 00:00:10,656
Strike a match. There is a flame.

2
00:00:10,736 --> 00:00:14,655
Leave the yeast out of the dough,
and the loaf comes out flat.

3
00:00:15,457 --> 00:00:20,571
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:21,389 --> 00:00:25,493
Nothing seems more certain than
that one thing brings about another.

5
00:00:25,573 --> 00:00:29,855
Rice grows from rice seed, never
from barley. Medicine heals.

6
00:00:29,935 --> 00:00:31,463
Actions bear fruit.

7
00:00:32,278 --> 00:00:34,970
But a quieter habit comes
with this certainty.

8
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:37,878
We picture the match as
holding a power to light.

9
00:00:37,958 --> 00:00:41,111
We picture the seed as
holding the sprout inside it,

10
00:00:41,191 --> 00:00:44,359
and the angry word as
holding the anger it causes.

11
00:00:44,439 --> 00:00:47,416
The cause becomes a little
thing with a force in it,

12
00:00:47,496 --> 00:00:51,822
and the effect becomes a second thing
that receives what was handed over.

13
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:55,812
That picture is the same
habit that builds a self.

14
00:00:55,892 --> 00:00:58,326
A self is the doer behind the doing.

15
00:00:58,406 --> 00:01:01,437
A causal power is the
doer behind the causing.

16
00:01:01,517 --> 00:01:05,798
When anatta is seen, the doer
behind seeing falls away.

17
00:01:05,878 --> 00:01:10,459
When this insight is seen, the
doer falls away from everything:

18
00:01:10,539 --> 00:01:14,403
the seed, the match,
the action, the moment.

19
00:01:15,222 --> 00:01:18,756
So this is my view, in
one line. Causes work.

20
00:01:18,836 --> 00:01:24,141
A power inside them that makes the
effect is never found. Both stand.

21
00:01:24,957 --> 00:01:27,055
Let me take the two halves in turn.

22
00:01:27,919 --> 00:01:29,646
First, causes work.

23
00:01:29,726 --> 00:01:32,133
Nothing in this stops
you lighting the stove.

24
00:01:32,213 --> 00:01:35,434
Barley seeds grow barley, and fire burns.

25
00:01:35,514 --> 00:01:38,070
The order of the world is untouched.

26
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:42,893
What goes is only one picture: a finished
thing being pushed across an edge by

27
00:01:42,973 --> 00:01:44,365
another finished thing.

28
00:01:45,186 --> 00:01:48,435
Second, no power is found. Take a key.

29
00:01:48,515 --> 00:01:50,758
It opens this lock and no other.

30
00:01:50,838 --> 00:01:53,652
Put it in the wrong lock,
and it opens nothing.

31
00:01:53,732 --> 00:01:57,104
So where is its power to
open? Not in the key alone.

32
00:01:57,184 --> 00:01:59,767
It shows itself only with its partner.

33
00:01:59,847 --> 00:02:04,825
A power that shows itself only with
its partner is not an inner property.

34
00:02:05,638 --> 00:02:06,781
Or take a seed.

35
00:02:06,861 --> 00:02:11,469
To say a seed grows because it has the
power to grow is to say it grows because

36
00:02:11,549 --> 00:02:16,908
it grows. The word "power" adds
a name, not an explanation.

37
00:02:17,725 --> 00:02:21,816
It helps to see that the word
"cause" is used in three ways.

38
00:02:21,896 --> 00:02:26,327
The first is a producer: something
existing by itself that makes an effect

39
00:02:26,407 --> 00:02:30,661
outside itself. That is
the one Nāgārjuna refuses.

40
00:02:30,741 --> 00:02:35,430
The second is a condition that lines up:
factors that let a result appear when they

41
00:02:35,510 --> 00:02:37,685
meet. That one stands.

42
00:02:37,765 --> 00:02:42,482
The third is a name: "cause" is what we
call the condition that attention picks

43
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:44,791
out when it follows a process.

44
00:02:44,871 --> 00:02:49,565
Keeping the third in view stops the
second from sliding back into the first.

45
00:02:50,369 --> 00:02:52,558
Now turn the usual worry round.

46
00:02:52,638 --> 00:02:57,286
People fear that if things are empty,
nothing could work. It is the other way.

47
00:02:57,366 --> 00:03:01,973
Suppose this moment existed by
itself, complete from its own side.

48
00:03:02,053 --> 00:03:06,702
Could it change? It could not,
because to change is to become other,

49
00:03:06,782 --> 00:03:09,596
and a nature of its own
does not become other.

50
00:03:09,676 --> 00:03:11,389
Could it combine with anything?

51
00:03:11,469 --> 00:03:14,800
No, because it depends
on nothing. Could it act?

52
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:19,039
No, because to act is to make a
difference to what is not itself.

53
00:03:19,119 --> 00:03:23,432
A world of things with their own
nature would be fixed, like an anvil.

54
00:03:23,521 --> 00:03:26,185
Things work, and what
works is found empty.

55
00:03:26,265 --> 00:03:28,794
And emptiness itself causes nothing.

56
00:03:28,874 --> 00:03:32,073
It is only what dependence
comes to when it is examined.

57
00:03:32,877 --> 00:03:35,161
Now the part I most want to make clear.

58
00:03:35,241 --> 00:03:36,945
Conditions are the appearing.

59
00:03:37,753 --> 00:03:42,007
Even after the power is gone,
the mind keeps one last layer.

60
00:03:42,087 --> 00:03:46,165
It pictures the conditions as
little things lined up underneath,

61
00:03:46,245 --> 00:03:49,860
which come together and then
give rise to the appearing.

62
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:52,224
Spark, fuel and air first.

63
00:03:52,304 --> 00:03:54,770
The flame afterwards, built out of them.

64
00:03:55,602 --> 00:03:56,827
But look at the flame.

65
00:03:56,907 --> 00:04:02,520
It is not assembled from spark, fuel and
air the way a wall is built from bricks.

66
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,400
What is there is the
burning, vivid and whole.

67
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:09,521
Spark, fuel and air are that
same appearing, divided up.

68
00:04:10,356 --> 00:04:14,189
Who divides it? A way of looking
that wants to explain something,

69
00:04:14,269 --> 00:04:17,164
or get something done.
Think of a loaf of bread.

70
00:04:17,244 --> 00:04:19,583
A cook says it rose because of the yeast,

71
00:04:19,663 --> 00:04:21,349
the warmth and the time.

72
00:04:21,429 --> 00:04:25,602
A chemist names the sugars,
the enzymes and the gas.

73
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:29,175
A physicist names molecules,
energy and pressure.

74
00:04:29,255 --> 00:04:32,980
A baker in a cold kitchen names
the draught by the window.

75
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,308
Each picks out different
conditions, and each works.

76
00:04:36,388 --> 00:04:40,330
None of them is the list of parts
the loaf was truly made from,

77
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:42,006
waiting to be read off.

78
00:04:42,869 --> 00:04:47,531
The parts appear as parts only in relation
to a framework that breaks appearances

79
00:04:47,611 --> 00:04:51,417
into parts, for explaining
and for getting things done.

80
00:04:51,497 --> 00:04:55,901
And that framework works within a
set of agreements, inside a setting.

81
00:04:55,981 --> 00:05:00,656
In a kitchen, leave out the yeast
and the loaf is flat, every time.

82
00:05:00,736 --> 00:05:04,841
Take the cook's account to the scale
of atoms, and it explains nothing.

83
00:05:04,921 --> 00:05:08,034
Take Newton to the speed
of light, and it fails.

84
00:05:08,114 --> 00:05:11,376
So the reliability is
enough to stake a life on.

85
00:05:11,456 --> 00:05:14,501
But it belongs to the framework
working in its setting,

86
00:05:14,581 --> 00:05:17,318
not to parts that exist
from their own side.

87
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:20,217
Then see what this does to causation.

88
00:05:20,297 --> 00:05:23,831
If the conditions are the
appearing, cut up for a purpose,

89
00:05:23,911 --> 00:05:28,342
then "the conditions produce the
appearing" turns out to be the appearing,

90
00:05:28,422 --> 00:05:31,155
divided, said to produce itself.

91
00:05:31,235 --> 00:05:35,964
The picture of production has nothing
left to stand on. And nothing is lost.

92
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:39,827
The cook still bakes. The
engineer still repairs the engine.

93
00:05:40,666 --> 00:05:42,434
Two wrong ways to hear this.

94
00:05:42,514 --> 00:05:45,410
One: so the conditions are only concepts,

95
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:51,007
and nothing really happens. No. The
framework works. That is the whole point.

96
00:05:51,087 --> 00:05:55,002
Two: so the appearing is
the true whole underneath,

97
00:05:55,082 --> 00:05:58,317
and the parts are
illusions laid on it. No.

98
00:05:58,397 --> 00:06:01,062
The whole and the parts
are named together,

99
00:06:01,142 --> 00:06:03,784
and neither is found standing by itself.

100
00:06:04,585 --> 00:06:09,536
Is this orthodox? Let me check it
against Nāgārjuna and his readers.

101
00:06:10,362 --> 00:06:12,796
The Middle Way opens with four corners.

102
00:06:12,876 --> 00:06:16,655
Not from itself, not from
another, not from both,

103
00:06:16,735 --> 00:06:21,804
and not without a cause: no thing
anywhere is ever found to have arisen.

104
00:06:21,884 --> 00:06:26,736
I read this as Candrakīrti does:
all four answers are refused,

105
00:06:26,816 --> 00:06:29,318
and no fifth is put in their place.

106
00:06:29,398 --> 00:06:34,345
Nāgārjuna also refuses a producing
activity inside the cause.

107
00:06:34,425 --> 00:06:37,089
That is exactly what I
mean by causal power.

108
00:06:37,169 --> 00:06:40,962
And he says conditions are called
conditions because something arises in

109
00:06:41,042 --> 00:06:45,205
dependence on them. A seed
in a dry jar is just a seed.

110
00:06:46,017 --> 00:06:49,999
In his twentieth chapter,
Nāgārjuna looks at the handover.

111
00:06:50,079 --> 00:06:53,885
If the cause gives its power
to the effect and then ceases,

112
00:06:53,965 --> 00:06:56,249
the cause would have two selves.

113
00:06:56,329 --> 00:07:00,298
If it ceases without giving,
the effect has no cause.

114
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:05,121
And if effect and cause were one,
producer and produced would be the same.

115
00:07:05,201 --> 00:07:09,456
If they were separate, a cause would
be no different from a non-cause.

116
00:07:09,536 --> 00:07:12,123
So nothing passes from cause to effect.

117
00:07:12,925 --> 00:07:17,179
One caution here. When I say
cause and effect arise together,

118
00:07:17,259 --> 00:07:20,698
I mean they are named together,
as long and short are.

119
00:07:20,778 --> 00:07:23,225
I do not mean they happen
at the same moment.

120
00:07:23,305 --> 00:07:27,138
In the world's terms, the
seed comes before the sprout.

121
00:07:27,218 --> 00:07:33,026
Nāgārjuna refuses a cause and effect
that sit side by side, and so do I.

122
00:07:33,833 --> 00:07:39,242
Candrakīrti refuses production from
another even in the world's own terms.

123
00:07:39,322 --> 00:07:43,114
Someone who plants a seed
says, "I planted this tree."

124
00:07:43,194 --> 00:07:45,967
They hold no theory of
two separate things.

125
00:07:46,047 --> 00:07:50,890
What the world uses is mere arising,
not production from its own side.

126
00:07:51,706 --> 00:07:54,140
Tsongkhapa adds a careful point.

127
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:58,868
In his school, a functioning thing is
defined as that which is able to perform a

128
00:07:58,948 --> 00:08:03,216
function. So he keeps a
capacity, in the world's terms:

129
00:08:03,296 --> 00:08:05,784
the seed is able to give a sprout.

130
00:08:05,864 --> 00:08:09,874
What he refuses is a capacity
that exists from its own side.

131
00:08:09,954 --> 00:08:14,534
Some of my older lines leaned towards
saying there is no capacity at all,

132
00:08:14,614 --> 00:08:17,455
only patterns. I would
now put it this way.

133
00:08:17,535 --> 00:08:20,023
No power is found from its own side.

134
00:08:20,103 --> 00:08:23,420
The capacity, named in dependence, works.

135
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,136
The key opens this lock.

136
00:08:25,945 --> 00:08:31,096
And this is not the philosopher Hume, who
dropped the power but kept the events,

137
00:08:31,176 --> 00:08:34,696
each standing alone, linked only by habit.

138
00:08:34,776 --> 00:08:38,220
For me there were never two
separate things that needed a link.

139
00:08:39,029 --> 00:08:43,405
Now the hardest part: karma
across time. An action ceases.

140
00:08:43,485 --> 00:08:45,556
How does its fruit come years later?

141
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:51,025
Tsongkhapa answers that the action's
having-ceased is itself a functioning

142
00:08:51,105 --> 00:08:54,970
thing. And its imprints are
said to rest on the mere I:

143
00:08:55,059 --> 00:08:58,525
the I that is only named
on the body and mind,

144
00:08:58,605 --> 00:09:03,176
not found among them, yet able
to act and to meet the result.

145
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:07,386
I keep the mere I as the
person the world speaks of.

146
00:09:07,489 --> 00:09:09,936
"I did it, and I will meet the result."

147
00:09:10,016 --> 00:09:14,039
That is a sound account of
responsibility, ethics and karma.

148
00:09:14,119 --> 00:09:18,903
What I refuse is the mere I as a bridge:
the thing that must be there for the

149
00:09:18,983 --> 00:09:23,065
imprints to rest on, so that
an action can reach its fruit.

150
00:09:23,941 --> 00:09:26,279
First, a bridge does not explain.

151
00:09:26,359 --> 00:09:28,417
It only passes the problem on.

152
00:09:28,547 --> 00:09:34,255
"Neither carried nor cut" is close to
Tsongkhapa's own refusal of the storehouse

153
00:09:34,335 --> 00:09:38,752
consciousness. Once we start
adding a layer to explain karma,

154
00:09:38,832 --> 00:09:42,448
rebirth or continuity,
there is no end to it.

155
00:09:42,528 --> 00:09:47,271
Ask of any carrier: does it last,
or does it change moment by moment?

156
00:09:47,351 --> 00:09:50,722
If it lasts, it cannot
take in changing imprints.

157
00:09:50,802 --> 00:09:54,717
If it changes, each of its own
moments has to get to the next,

158
00:09:54,797 --> 00:09:57,656
and that needs another carrier. And so on.

159
00:09:58,488 --> 00:10:02,104
Tsongkhapa's having-ceased
is momentary too,

160
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:05,052
a continuum that runs until the fruit.

161
00:10:05,132 --> 00:10:08,938
If each of its moments follows
the next with no further link,

162
00:10:09,018 --> 00:10:13,752
then the action's own sequence needs
no link either. Nothing has been added.

163
00:10:14,569 --> 00:10:16,749
Where does the need
for a bridge come from?

164
00:10:16,838 --> 00:10:19,502
From the habit of the inherent framework:

165
00:10:19,582 --> 00:10:24,122
moments taken as things standing on
their own, with a gap between them.

166
00:10:24,202 --> 00:10:27,306
Experiential reality is never like that.

167
00:10:27,436 --> 00:10:31,377
"Neither carried nor cut"
offers no other way across.

168
00:10:31,457 --> 00:10:35,114
It denies both: that the
act travels to the fruit,

169
00:10:35,194 --> 00:10:38,551
and that the act ends in
nothing before the fruit comes.

170
00:10:38,631 --> 00:10:40,453
It puts nothing in their place.

171
00:10:40,533 --> 00:10:43,442
That the fruit follows the
act was never a riddle.

172
00:10:43,522 --> 00:10:45,467
Rice still comes from rice seed.

173
00:10:45,547 --> 00:10:48,053
Only the demand for a bridge has to go.

174
00:10:48,869 --> 00:10:51,103
Dōgen says it from the other side.

175
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:55,922
Firewood burns to ash, and ash
does not turn back into firewood.

176
00:10:56,002 --> 00:10:59,944
Yet do not think of firewood
as before and ash as after.

177
00:11:00,024 --> 00:11:02,348
We do not say winter becomes spring.

178
00:11:02,428 --> 00:11:05,840
Winter is wholly winter,
spring wholly spring,

179
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:08,209
and no winter-stuff crosses over.

180
00:11:08,339 --> 00:11:11,873
Firewood stays in its own
place, fully firewood;

181
00:11:11,953 --> 00:11:14,713
ash in its own place, fully ash.

182
00:11:14,793 --> 00:11:19,658
Before and after are cut off, but
this is not the cut of annihilation:

183
00:11:19,738 --> 00:11:22,552
nothing that existed was
destroyed into nothing.

184
00:11:22,632 --> 00:11:26,044
And the order holds:
firewood burns to ash,

185
00:11:26,124 --> 00:11:27,756
never the other way round.

186
00:11:27,836 --> 00:11:30,460
Nothing travels, so nothing is carried.

187
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:33,612
Nothing falls into
nothing, so nothing is cut.

188
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:36,144
And the fruit still follows the act.

189
00:11:36,958 --> 00:11:42,503
There is a second reason. Tsongkhapa
himself rejects a mind that knows itself,

190
00:11:42,583 --> 00:11:44,568
even in the world's terms.

191
00:11:44,648 --> 00:11:49,990
It was posited to explain memory, and he
says it is a theory built to fill a gap,

192
00:11:50,070 --> 00:11:51,946
not something the world knows.

193
00:11:52,026 --> 00:11:56,539
When the mere I is asked to be the
bridge for karma, it does the same job.

194
00:11:56,619 --> 00:12:01,308
It fills the gap. The world does
say "I did it", so the person stays.

195
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:02,911
Only the bridge goes.

196
00:12:02,991 --> 00:12:06,824
And the having-ceased of an
action, as a functioning thing,

197
00:12:06,904 --> 00:12:09,107
is even more clearly a theory.

198
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:11,122
No one in the world knows of it.

199
00:12:11,954 --> 00:12:15,230
So I keep the phrase
"neither carried nor cut".

200
00:12:15,310 --> 00:12:18,573
Nothing is carried across,
and nothing is cut off.

201
00:12:18,653 --> 00:12:20,855
It is not meant as a better theory.

202
00:12:20,935 --> 00:12:22,952
It is meant to make you face something.

203
00:12:23,753 --> 00:12:25,643
It leaves the mind uneasy.

204
00:12:25,723 --> 00:12:29,393
Something seems to be missing
between the act and its fruit.

205
00:12:29,473 --> 00:12:34,991
Do not answer that feeling. Look at it,
again and again, until you see what it is.

206
00:12:35,071 --> 00:12:39,896
The gap is felt only because the habit of
seeing things as existing in themselves

207
00:12:39,976 --> 00:12:41,730
needs something to be there.

208
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:46,336
Analysis shows, every time,
that no bridge can be found.

209
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:49,379
Moment-to-moment
experience never meets one.

210
00:12:49,459 --> 00:12:51,458
And still the feeling returns.

211
00:12:51,538 --> 00:12:55,099
That shows how deep the habit
of confused seeing runs,

212
00:12:55,179 --> 00:12:58,419
though no power to blind is ever found.

213
00:12:59,229 --> 00:13:02,083
And when the dismantling
has nowhere left to go,

214
00:13:02,163 --> 00:13:08,163
no bridge, and no break either, then with
nothing left to link, nothing is missing.

215
00:13:09,169 --> 00:13:12,934
That is where you can glimpse what
Dzogchen calls being beyond cause and

216
00:13:13,014 --> 00:13:17,227
effect. I do not read it as a
place where causes stop working.

217
00:13:17,307 --> 00:13:21,901
I read it as the end of the demand
for a producer, and for a final why.

218
00:13:21,981 --> 00:13:25,013
The display is complete
and present as it is,

219
00:13:25,093 --> 00:13:27,445
owing nothing to anything behind it.

220
00:13:27,525 --> 00:13:29,555
Nothing higher, nothing lower.

221
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:33,817
Here I part from some readings,
and I want to say so plainly.

222
00:13:33,897 --> 00:13:39,062
Many Dzogchen texts describe spontaneous
presence as the presence of the ground,

223
00:13:39,142 --> 00:13:41,834
not made by causes and conditions.

224
00:13:41,914 --> 00:13:46,236
I read spontaneous presence
as dependent arising itself,

225
00:13:46,316 --> 00:13:48,423
met without the habit of fixing.

226
00:13:48,503 --> 00:13:51,657
Not uncaused, and not
a source behind things.

227
00:13:51,737 --> 00:13:53,428
That is my own synthesis.

228
00:13:54,249 --> 00:13:59,739
It is closest to Mipham, who holds
that appearance and emptiness are one,

229
00:13:59,819 --> 00:14:02,674
and who uses analysis to bring certainty.

230
00:14:02,754 --> 00:14:05,324
But on bridges, Mipham and I part.

231
00:14:05,404 --> 00:14:10,677
He keeps a mind that knows itself,
in the world's terms. I am stricter.

232
00:14:10,757 --> 00:14:15,650
Even so, his self-knowing is not a
second act turned back on the first.

233
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:19,875
It is the clarity of knowing,
not lit by anything else.

234
00:14:19,955 --> 00:14:24,173
And that is very near what I mean
when I say clarity is never missing.

235
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:26,629
So how is this seen through?

236
00:14:26,709 --> 00:14:28,925
Not by a better theory of causes.

237
00:14:29,005 --> 00:14:31,751
By looking for the power
and not finding it,

238
00:14:31,831 --> 00:14:34,201
and then seeing that nothing was lost.

239
00:14:35,009 --> 00:14:39,766
Strike a match and look for the moment
the flame passes from not being to being.

240
00:14:39,846 --> 00:14:43,371
At no moment is a finished
flame handed across.

241
00:14:44,194 --> 00:14:45,681
Or take angry words.

242
00:14:45,811 --> 00:14:50,555
"Your words made me angry." The anger
arose with the words, the hearing,

243
00:14:50,635 --> 00:14:53,150
an old hurt and a tired evening.

244
00:14:53,230 --> 00:14:56,193
No power to anger sits inside the words.

245
00:14:56,273 --> 00:14:58,571
Yet the words can be apologised for.

246
00:14:58,651 --> 00:15:01,084
This is where the insight matters most.

247
00:15:01,164 --> 00:15:04,440
Suffering is kept going by
conditions that can change,

248
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:06,890
not by a power that must be fought.

249
00:15:07,705 --> 00:15:10,383
When this is seen, the search for a power,

250
00:15:10,463 --> 00:15:12,815
a carrier and a ground stops.

251
00:15:12,895 --> 00:15:17,801
The last why stops applying, though "why
did the loaf fail?" still has its answer.

252
00:15:17,881 --> 00:15:20,600
Conditions matter more, not less.

253
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:24,581
And appearing is met as
it is: vivid, working,

254
00:15:24,661 --> 00:15:27,978
complete, and not found
standing by itself.

255
00:15:28,058 --> 00:15:31,361
Mind and matter lose their
weight, and become light,

256
00:15:31,441 --> 00:15:33,431
magical and plastic.

257
00:15:34,242 --> 00:15:36,934
Why does this problem
never come up in seeing?

258
00:15:37,014 --> 00:15:42,138
In the seen, just the seen, the question
of how the act reaches its fruit does not

259
00:15:42,218 --> 00:15:45,494
arise. Not because experience answers it.

260
00:15:45,574 --> 00:15:48,243
The question needs a
split that is not there.

261
00:15:49,065 --> 00:15:51,702
It needs two things standing on their own,

262
00:15:51,782 --> 00:15:54,977
a before and an after,
with a gap between them.

263
00:15:55,057 --> 00:15:57,205
In seeing, neither is found.

264
00:15:57,285 --> 00:15:58,998
Each instant is complete.

265
00:15:59,078 --> 00:16:02,562
The seeing is wholly seeing,
the sound wholly sound.

266
00:16:03,373 --> 00:16:05,589
It needs someone outside, looking.

267
00:16:05,669 --> 00:16:10,236
To see a gap between two moments,
there must be a place outside both.

268
00:16:10,316 --> 00:16:12,056
That place is the observer.

269
00:16:12,136 --> 00:16:16,486
When anatta is seen, there
is no seer behind the seeing,

270
00:16:16,566 --> 00:16:19,697
and in the same move no
causer behind the causing.

271
00:16:20,513 --> 00:16:22,933
And it needs time as something on its own.

272
00:16:23,013 --> 00:16:25,922
Past and future are never met as places.

273
00:16:26,002 --> 00:16:31,280
Remembering is this appearing, now,
as its conditions come together.

274
00:16:32,085 --> 00:16:34,532
So the gap is never found in looking.

275
00:16:34,612 --> 00:16:38,771
It comes in when thought lines the
instants up and asks how one gets to the

276
00:16:38,851 --> 00:16:43,051
next. Without that framework,
it is one complete stroke.

277
00:16:43,131 --> 00:16:47,657
This is not a oneness: seeing
is seeing, hearing is hearing,

278
00:16:47,737 --> 00:16:50,170
with no pure consciousness behind them.

279
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:52,113
And it is not a state to keep up.

280
00:16:52,193 --> 00:16:53,948
Maintenance is the split.

281
00:16:54,028 --> 00:16:58,504
Clarity is never absent; it
is only not abstracted out.

282
00:16:59,305 --> 00:17:00,583
Try it with the gap.

283
00:17:00,663 --> 00:17:04,279
Recall something you did years ago
whose result you live with now.

284
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:08,301
Notice the feeling of a missing
gap between then and now.

285
00:17:08,381 --> 00:17:11,331
Look at that feeling. Is
the gap found anywhere?

286
00:17:11,411 --> 00:17:14,102
Stay with it until the asking loosens.

287
00:17:14,182 --> 00:17:16,186
The act still bore its fruit.

288
00:17:16,997 --> 00:17:21,441
And one more. Try it. Turn on
a tap. Watch the water come.

289
00:17:21,521 --> 00:17:24,553
Look for the moment the
tap makes the water flow.

290
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:26,998
Then look for the flowing
apart from the tap,

291
00:17:27,078 --> 00:17:31,541
the pipe, the pressure and the turn
of your hand. Neither is found.

292
00:17:32,361 --> 00:17:34,147
And the water still flows.

